From: MyWirelessAndroidAutoDongle contributors
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: give RX preallocation definitions strict prototypes

Clang 23 rejects the two empty parameter lists under the kernel's
-Werror=strict-prototypes check. Match the existing (void) declarations
in aicwf_rx_prealloc.h without changing behavior or disabling diagnostics.

Apply to the fc7cbdd1791416c2457fa27a59e508bf325c9c3f SDK after Radxa's
Debian patch series and the scoped monitor callback compatibility patch.
---
--- a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_rx_prealloc.c
+++ b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_rx_prealloc.c
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
     spin_unlock_irqrestore(lock, flags);
 }
 
-int aicwf_prealloc_init()
+int aicwf_prealloc_init(void)
 {
     struct rx_buff *rxbuff;
     int i = 0;
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@
     return 0;
 }
 
-void aicwf_prealloc_exit()
+void aicwf_prealloc_exit(void)
 {
     struct rx_buff *rxbuff;
     struct rx_buff *pos;
